Job Description
 At Fugro, we unlock insights from geo-data to help clients design, build and operate their assets safely, sustainably and efficiently. As a global leader in Geo-data solutions, we combine world-class expertise with advanced digital technologies to tackle some of the world's biggest challenges in infrastructure, energy and water.
GroundIQ offers a revolutionary and efficient way to map and model the subsurface, making the process faster, more targeted and more sustainable. Next to the project business, GroundIQ is opening its platform to external users through software subscriptions, and building this recurring SaaS business is a key part of our growth strategy. To support this growth, we are looking for a GTM Engineer who will build and run our AI-native go-to-market operating system one engine that finds, qualifies and engages buyers, and learns from every outcome. If you enjoy combining AI agents, automation, integrations and CRM to turn market signals into customers, this is your opportunity to make a lasting impact within an innovative and entrepreneurial environment.
 Your role
You own and continuously improve our HubSpot ecosystem as the system of record of our go-to-market operating system, ensuring a scalable architecture, strong data governance, efficient pipelines, and a user-friendly experience across the business; 
You design and build the commercial foundation for GroundIQ, creating a scalable data model for products, subscriptions, customers and partners, and maintaining the GTM brain in Claude and GitHub that holds our playbooks and data; 
You create seamless lead management processes, implementing buying signals, lead capture, enrichment, fit and timing scoring and routing workflows that connect prospects with the right teams at the right time; 
You build and maintain integrations between business-critical systems, connecting HubSpot and Claude with our website, the GroundIQ platform, product usage data and Microsoft 365 through connectors, APIs, webhooks and automation tools; 
You automate the journey from free trial to renewal, helping establish subscription billing processes and reducing manual effort across quoting, contracting, invoicing and renewals; 
You develop customer lifecycle workflows, enabling Sales and Customer Success teams to manage onboarding, account health, renewals and growth opportunities based on platform usage and credit data; 
You build AI agents and automation to increase efficiency, taking over research, scoring and the drafting of outreach and replies, with a person approving every message, so commercial teams can focus on high-value activities; 
You deliver meaningful reporting and insights, creating dashboards and weekly reports that give leadership a clear view of pipeline performance, recurring revenue and customer growth, and feeding what works back into our playbooks; 
You act as the go-to expert for commercial systems, working with Fugro IT and security, training users, documenting processes and driving adoption across Sales, Marketing and Customer Success teams. 
 Your track record
You bring a minimum of 3 years of experience in GTM Engineering, RevOps, growth engineering or Marketing Operations, preferably within a B2B SaaS, software or scale-up environment; 
You are AI-native you work with tools such as Claude and Claude Code every day, and have built AI agents or agentic workflows that run in a real commercial process; 
You have hands-on experience with signal-based prospecting, enrichment and outreach, using tools such as Clay, HeyReach or comparable solutions; 
You are experienced with HubSpot or similar CRM solutions, and know how to keep data clean and well structured as the business grows; 
You have built integrations using APIs, webhooks and automation platforms, such as n8n, Make or Zapier, and are comfortable working with Python, SQL and GitHub; 
You have experience with subscription management and quote-to-cash processes, including billing platforms such as Stripe, Chargebee or comparable solutions; 
You combine technical expertise with strong stakeholder management skills, translating commercial requirements into working systems and expl
[...]
clearly to non-technical colleagues; 
You communicate fluently in English, while Dutch language skills are considered a plus. 
 What Fugro Offers
A competitive salary; 
29 holidays per year based on a fulltime employment (of which 4 are appointed by Fugro management) and the possibility to purchase 12 additional days; 
Extensive career & training opportunities both nationally and internationally; 
Flexible working hours and the ability to work from home in accordance with your manager and corporate policies; 
Commuting allowance; 
Modern pension scheme; 
Collective health insurance; 
Possibility to register with our corporate fitness plan; 
Coaching options through our EAP (Employee Assistance Program). 
 Are you interested?
 Please visit our Company Page to find out more on what it is like to work at Fugro.
If you have any further questions, please contact Umit Nesar, Corporate Recruiter, tel. +31 (0)6 - 81 41 07 68.
 After you have applied
You will receive an automated confirmation-email of the receipt of your application; 
When we see a match, we will invite you for the first interview within a couple of days. Of course, you will also receive a message if we will not invite you; 
After a successful first round, you will be invited for the second round; 
If we are both still positive after the second interview, we will make you an offer and with that we hope to welcome you at Fugro! 
 Disclaimer For Recruitment Agencies
 Fugro does not accept any unsolicited applications from recruitment agencies. Acquisition to Fugro Recruitment or any Fugro employee is not appreciated . 
